WEBVTT

00:01.680 --> 00:04.724
"It seems today that all you see

00:04.807 --> 00:08.270
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:08.353 --> 00:12.025
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:12.108 --> 00:14.192
"On which we used to rely?

00:14.944 --> 00:18.155
"Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.280 --> 00:23.160
"Lucky there's a man who positively
can do all the things that make us

00:23.286 --> 00:24.829
"Laugh and cry

00:24.954 --> 00:30.166
"He's a family guy

00:36.506 --> 00:39.343
Whoo-hoo, baby! 12 in a row!

00:40.678 --> 00:44.223
You must have had a great body
before it went all fun-house mirror.

00:44.348 --> 00:48.936
- I can't believe how terrific you look.
- I've been taking tae-jitsu classes.

00:49.020 --> 00:51.523
- You should come with me sometime.
- I'd love to.

00:51.648 --> 00:54.650
- Oh! The baby's kicking. Wanna feel?
- Sure.

00:57.152 --> 00:59.237
- You are freakin' dead, kid.
- Peter!

00:59.237 --> 01:02.492
- Oh, I love this time of year.
- Me, too.

01:02.575 --> 01:05.620
The tourists are gone and
we have the town to ourselves

01:05.704 --> 01:10.834
before those idiots from New York show up
to watch the leaves change and take over.

01:17.090 --> 01:18.758
Leafers!

01:18.841 --> 01:21.468
Holy crap. We gotta get outta here.

01:24.680 --> 01:27.183
- What about the boat?
- Leave it!

01:28.226 --> 01:32.813
- Hurry, Peter. They're almost here.
- We're too late.

01:32.938 --> 01:37.944
Yo, check out those colours. Yellow like
a taxi, orange like the ball at the Knicks game,

01:38.027 --> 01:40.864
and red like the sauce
on my mamma mia's gugotz.

01:40.947 --> 01:43.867
Yeah, and brown, like the guys
I don't pick up in my cab.

01:43.992 --> 01:46.494
- Bea-utiful!
- Aagh!

01:46.577 --> 01:48.663
Good evening. Tonight's top story:

01:48.788 --> 01:53.460
Quahog is infested with loud, hairy
creatures, also known as New Yorkers.

01:53.460 --> 01:56.297
They migrate north
every autumn to see the foliage.

01:56.380 --> 01:58.465
I think I speak for all of us when I say

01:58.590 --> 02:01.593
New Yorkers can fornicate
themselves with an iron stick.

02:05.138 --> 02:09.434
- We're gonna be late for church.
- Move it! Damn leafers.

02:09.518 --> 02:13.271
Christ, quit it! Mom,
Chris put his foot on my side again.

02:13.396 --> 02:17.442
- I can't help it. I have long dancer's legs.
- Move it.

02:17.567 --> 02:21.738
Stop whining. Stay on your side.
Lois, get off your ass and do some parenting.

02:21.822 --> 02:25.075
If you don't stop, we won't
go to McDonald's after church.

02:25.158 --> 02:27.869
- Mom!
- Don't worry. We're goin'.

02:29.538 --> 02:32.458
- But you don't get the Super Size.
- Oh!

02:32.583 --> 02:35.920
- OK, you can Super Size, but no apple pie.
- Come on.

02:36.003 --> 02:38.214
OK, but you can't blow on it.

02:38.297 --> 02:40.924
Peter, don't contradict me in front of the kids.

02:41.007 --> 02:45.929
Brothers and sisters fightin' is as natural as
a white man's dialogue in a Spike Lee movie.

02:46.013 --> 02:51.351
Wassup? Can I get two slices of pepperoni?

02:55.731 --> 02:58.109
- Who are all these people?
- Damn New Yorkers.

02:58.234 --> 03:00.318
They took all the good seats.

03:00.403 --> 03:02.488
Aren't you precious!

03:07.409 --> 03:11.580
Some of my novelty items
were provided by Jack's Joke Shop.

03:11.665 --> 03:14.082
If it ain't funny, it ain't worth Jack.

03:15.001 --> 03:18.045
I'd like to welcome
all our out-of-town parishioners.

03:18.129 --> 03:21.882
My cousin, Father Sapienza,
is in from New York to see the leaves.

03:22.007 --> 03:25.219
I'd like to invite him
to do the opening prayer.

03:25.344 --> 03:28.557
Yo, God is good, huh?
And he expects us to be good.

03:28.682 --> 03:32.851
And if you're not, he's gonna come down
and bust your freakin' skull. Amen.

03:32.935 --> 03:36.188
Who do you think you're talking to?
God ain't tougher than me.

03:36.271 --> 03:39.400
You can't talk to the father like that,
you stupid gavone.

03:39.525 --> 03:41.903
I oughta come and break your freakin' arm!

03:42.028 --> 03:45.364
Wanna go, tough guy?
I'll snap you in half like an almond biscotti

03:45.448 --> 03:48.576
from Valero's on 51st Street, best in the city.

03:48.576 --> 03:52.330
Fellas, this is God's house.
And the Patriots kick off in 45 minutes.

03:52.330 --> 03:54.958
- Can we move this along?
- Patriots suck.

03:55.041 --> 03:57.127
Blasphemy!

03:57.127 --> 03:59.002
It burns!

03:59.127 --> 04:02.047
Holy water? Where's that acid I ordered?

04:02.549 --> 04:05.385
Hey, Guido, watch this.

04:05.468 --> 04:08.930
Whoa! I've got to lay off the coffee.
Ha-cha-cha-cha-cha-cha!

04:09.014 --> 04:11.307
That's Jack's. Exit 14 off 295.

04:13.602 --> 04:17.272
Tae-jitsu is about power -
for your body and your mind.

04:17.355 --> 04:19.984
Don't be afraid to free the beast inside you.

04:20.067 --> 04:23.403
Left kick, right kick, punch combo, stomp.

04:23.528 --> 04:25.696
Beautiful. Again. Left kick...

04:25.821 --> 04:29.659
- You're doing great for your first lesson.
- I'm really cuttin' loose.

04:29.784 --> 04:33.121
Like Julie Andrews in that movie
where she showed her breasts.

04:33.205 --> 04:36.750
Mary, you'll never leave us, will you?

04:37.708 --> 04:40.503
Lovely, but it doesn't quite
answer our question.

04:46.343 --> 04:47.928
Jets rule!

04:50.430 --> 04:55.644
Watch where you're going. Horace, put the
Pats game on the TV and get me a few beers.

04:55.728 --> 04:58.647
Sorry, Peter. Someone stole the remotes.

04:58.772 --> 05:03.359
And the kegs. And I'm not sure,
but I think I've been shot.

05:03.443 --> 05:05.111
Yep.

05:05.236 --> 05:09.491
Hey, pal, watch my seat.
I gotta bleed the lizard.

05:11.576 --> 05:16.081
Public urination is just wrong.
Except during the Million Man March

05:16.165 --> 05:18.876
when protesters burned our Porta-Pottis.

05:19.001 --> 05:22.338
Then I used my stream of justice
to put out the hate.

05:22.421 --> 05:25.966
I don't know, fellas. I think
there's potential in this crowd.

05:26.091 --> 05:29.427
Honey, why don't you turn around
and show me the Lower East Side?

05:29.512 --> 05:31.597
- Sure.
- Transvestite! Back off.

05:31.597 --> 05:33.807
- Wait a sec. Pre-op or post-op?
- Pre-op.

05:33.890 --> 05:39.230
Transvestite! Back off. This place blows.
We gotta send these strap-hangers back.

05:39.313 --> 05:41.399
Don't worry. I got an idea.

05:41.399 --> 05:48.906
An idea so smart, my head would explode if I
even began to know what I was talking about.

05:52.577 --> 05:55.579
Aagh! I am a man-eating tree.

05:55.704 --> 05:58.499
Go back to New York or I will eat you.

05:58.499 --> 06:03.212
Just like I ate insane
New York anchorman Dan Rather. Pah!

06:03.296 --> 06:08.634
And look who I had for dessert.
Asexual former mayor Ed Koch. Pah!

06:08.717 --> 06:12.263
Leave my land or I will smite you
with my powerful limb.

06:12.388 --> 06:14.683
What are you, nuts? Give me that branch.

06:14.766 --> 06:16.850
Get off of me!

06:18.520 --> 06:21.230
Oh, my God! Stop fighting!

06:24.067 --> 06:26.861
- Holy crap!
- Oh, my God!

06:28.947 --> 06:31.157
Mom, you could be a world champion,

06:31.240 --> 06:35.536
and no one could hit you below the belt
cos girls don't have anything down there.

06:35.619 --> 06:39.498
- Can you teach me to kick ass?
- No. I do not condone violence.

06:39.581 --> 06:43.128
I won't be responsible for
bringing fistfighting into our schools.

06:43.253 --> 06:46.256
Gee, can you hear me
all the way back there in the '50s?

06:46.256 --> 06:49.717
- That was lame.
- Poor Peter.

06:49.800 --> 06:54.306
I emasculated him in front of all those people.
I think he's really upset.

06:54.389 --> 06:57.851
Gather round, everybody.
10 bucks is all it takes.

06:57.935 --> 07:00.437
Step right up and fight my wife.

07:03.898 --> 07:08.487
Come one, come all. She floats like a
butterfly and stings like when I pee.

07:08.570 --> 07:12.949
Peter, I am not a sideshow attraction.
At least, not any more.

07:13.909 --> 07:17.329
Me likey bouncy! Me likey bouncy!

07:17.454 --> 07:22.668
I want you to get rid of all of this right now,
cos I am never fighting again, ever!

07:22.752 --> 07:26.296
Come on, Chris. We'll have to go to plan B.

07:29.841 --> 07:32.969
No! Oh, God! Oh, my God!

07:32.969 --> 07:37.766
Help me! Help me!
For God's sake, he's gonna kill me!

07:37.891 --> 07:41.310
Don't worry. It's a trained bear.
He's in no real danger.

07:44.565 --> 07:47.693
He's teaching a class. I can't bother him now.

07:47.776 --> 07:52.155
Sure you can. Hey, Ralph Macchio!
My wife here needs to talk to you.

07:52.280 --> 07:53.824
There you go, honey.

07:53.949 --> 07:58.119
- What is it, Lois?
- I don't think I should do tae-jitsu any more.

07:58.202 --> 08:02.083
- I'm afraid I'm gonna hurt someone.
- But, Lois, you're my star pupil.

08:02.167 --> 08:06.044
- I want you in my advanced class.
- Advanced class? No, no, no.

08:06.128 --> 08:08.839
- I'm trying to quit.
- Well, fine. Quit.

08:08.964 --> 08:12.384
- But get used to people walking all over you.
- Hold on, there.

08:12.509 --> 08:15.304
Nobody walks all over my wife,
cos I won't let 'em.

08:15.429 --> 08:17.389
- Peter...
- Quiet. Men are talking.

08:17.514 --> 08:21.143
She learns things eventually.
It just takes her longer. Come on.

08:21.268 --> 08:25.648
If you hurry, I'll let you try on hats.
I won't let you buy, but you can try 'em on.

08:25.731 --> 08:27.108
I'll do it.

08:38.786 --> 08:40.872
Ow!

08:45.959 --> 08:49.714
- Stewie, you wanna swing?
- Yes, why not? I'll have a go at it.

08:49.839 --> 08:52.550
Perhaps a quick stretch first.

08:54.094 --> 08:57.429
Damn. Must have pulled something
playing hoops last week.

08:58.681 --> 09:03.060
I know you're not puttin' that rock
up from here. You ain't got no J.

09:05.771 --> 09:09.026
- Yo, man, that's trippin'!
- You're the one who's trippin'.

09:09.109 --> 09:11.318
Cry home to your mama. She waitin' for ya.

09:11.402 --> 09:14.322
Now don't make me put
my size 13s up your narrow ass!

09:14.447 --> 09:18.201
I don't sweat you. Bring it on, bitch!
Now how you gonna act?

09:18.285 --> 09:21.955
Sheesh! Bringin' that trash in here.
This is my house.

09:23.415 --> 09:26.125
Excuse me. We were about to use that.

09:26.209 --> 09:29.254
- You snooze, you lose, lady.
- You have two choices.

09:29.337 --> 09:32.882
Either my baby swings from
this jungle gym, or you do.

09:34.259 --> 09:38.012
Ooh, Lois! Someone's wearing
their ovaries on the outside.

09:38.096 --> 09:41.141
- She saw me walking to the swing.
- She saw you. Easy, now.

09:41.224 --> 09:45.937
Nobody walks all over me. Those days
are over. Lois Griffin demands respect.

09:48.524 --> 09:53.236
I smell a messy diaper.
God, why does that turn me on?

09:56.781 --> 09:59.493
- Hold it, Meg. Those two are mine.
- What?

09:59.576 --> 10:04.997
That's Randy, and that's Fred.
Randy is the messy one. Fred's very neat.

10:04.997 --> 10:09.085
When you get 'em together,
hold on to your sides!

10:09.711 --> 10:12.088
Nice to meet you both.

10:12.840 --> 10:14.925
Murderer!

10:15.634 --> 10:19.388
Stop it, both of you. Starting now,
you two are gonna love each other.

10:19.513 --> 10:21.598
Now stay that way.

10:22.725 --> 10:24.935
It's gonna be weird to potty.

10:25.853 --> 10:29.398
Sheesh, Lois, look at the garbage
those damn leafers dumped on our lawn.

10:29.523 --> 10:33.151
New York Post, New York Magazine,
the New York Mets.

10:33.276 --> 10:37.948
Peter, I'm sick and tired of hearing you whine
about the leafers. Take some action.

10:38.073 --> 10:40.159
Free the beast!

10:43.912 --> 10:47.040
That was strangely arousing. Aagh!

10:49.835 --> 10:54.423
Hello? 911? It's Quagmire.
Yeah. It's in a window this time.

10:54.423 --> 10:59.637
- Wow, look at them run.
- Wait a second, Brian. That gives me an idea.

11:03.807 --> 11:09.438
The Drunken Clam? Why couldn't we go
someplace fancy, like The Olive Garden?

11:09.563 --> 11:13.401
The breadsticks!
Me likey breadsticks! Me likey...

11:13.401 --> 11:16.529
- You're a big girl now. Stop it.
- Hold on, Lois.

11:16.654 --> 11:21.534
Excuse me, New Yorker. You're in my seat,
and I had sex with your mother last night.

11:21.659 --> 11:23.743
- Are you crazy?
- What did you say?

11:23.827 --> 11:26.956
About the seat, or about
my ploughing your father's wife?

11:26.956 --> 11:30.919
- What the hell are you doing?
- Excuse me. Is your refrigerator running?

11:31.044 --> 11:35.298
If it is, it probably runs like you -
very homosexually.

11:35.298 --> 11:37.800
- What?!
- Oh, you wanna dance?

11:38.760 --> 11:41.471
Jets suck, Yankees suck, Knicks suck.

11:45.642 --> 11:47.727
Krypton sucks.

12:01.491 --> 12:05.870
That's right. Go back where
you came from, you bastards!

12:10.876 --> 12:15.130
We'll conclude the graduation ceremony
with a demonstration by the black belts.

12:15.130 --> 12:17.215
Let's show 'em what we've learnt.

12:17.340 --> 12:20.969
- Kathy, get in there with Lois.
- I can't. I have cramps.

12:21.094 --> 12:23.472
Why are you putting me up
against the scrubs?

12:23.597 --> 12:28.601
- Be a man and fight me yourself.
- Lois, the sensei is a sacred position.

12:28.684 --> 12:33.190
I could never violate the spiritual bond
of the student-master relationship.

12:33.273 --> 12:35.775
- Then allow me.
- Ooh!

12:35.900 --> 12:39.529
- The bond is broken.
- Then spin the wheel, raggedy man!

12:39.654 --> 12:43.909
Go, Lois! Pummel him
with your powerful fists of female fury.

12:43.909 --> 12:47.787
And then when he's weary,
emasculate him with your incessant nagging.

12:47.871 --> 12:50.791
Women! Yakety-yak, yakety-yak, yak, yak.

12:50.791 --> 12:53.626
You know, huh? Enjoy the fight.

13:07.598 --> 13:09.351
Yah!

13:09.476 --> 13:12.896
Lois, that was amazing. Congratu...

13:13.021 --> 13:16.985
This is mine.
This is where my babies come from.

13:18.652 --> 13:21.571
And now back to the movie of the week.

13:23.324 --> 13:27.077
If this glacier goes slower
than one mile a year, we're all dead!

13:27.077 --> 13:30.331
Tell me something I don't know!
Get out of the way!

13:34.084 --> 13:36.671
Lois, I was watching that.

13:37.713 --> 13:40.841
- What you looking at?
- The underpants. Lose 'em.

13:40.966 --> 13:44.386
Actually, I kinda...
I sorta have a headache, kinda.

13:44.511 --> 13:46.888
- Maybe tomorrow or...
- Take 'em off.

13:47.013 --> 13:48.474
Yeah, OK, honey.

13:52.311 --> 13:55.773
Whoa! What the hell are you doing?
Those are my graham crackers.

13:55.856 --> 13:58.901
Run along, Stewie. Daddy had a rough night.

13:58.985 --> 14:01.905
Why, you tottering, fem-sucked dewberry!

14:02.030 --> 14:06.409
I'm going to go find something
to strike you with. Excuse me.

14:06.492 --> 14:10.247
Good morning.
Peter, you look terrible. What happened?

14:10.372 --> 14:14.209
Last night Lois was... the man!

14:14.334 --> 14:18.713
- Good Lord.
- I just want you to know, Brian, I didn't cry.

14:18.797 --> 14:21.925
It's OK. Shh.

14:24.761 --> 14:28.097
Oh, no! Peter! Stewie, what did you do?

14:28.181 --> 14:31.017
He freed the beast
all over the back of Peter's head.

14:31.101 --> 14:33.729
Oh, my God. This is my fault.

14:33.812 --> 14:37.065
This is my fault!
I brought violence into this house!

14:37.148 --> 14:40.902
- I'm the worst mother in the world!
- Ah-ha! I got it all on tape.

14:42.278 --> 14:45.823
OK, this is me
interviewing Ed Sullivan.

14:45.907 --> 14:47.493
What's new, Ed?

14:47.576 --> 14:51.745
Well, Stewie,
tonight we have a really big show.

14:51.871 --> 14:54.874
OK, and now a word
from our sponsors.

14:54.874 --> 14:58.837
It takes a very steady hand.
Don't touch the sides!

14:58.837 --> 15:01.340
Butterfingers!

15:01.465 --> 15:04.050
I was making radio shows for fun.

15:04.050 --> 15:08.429
Everybody does it.
At least, everybody I know. Shut up!

15:12.809 --> 15:18.440
Stewart, take this mommy doll and daddy
doll and show me how they act together.

15:18.440 --> 15:21.151
Oh. Yes, very well. All right.

15:22.318 --> 15:27.533
"Margaret, after 20 years of marriage, your
curious indiscretions no longer faze me. "

15:27.616 --> 15:30.535
"Really? And I suppose
you think I enjoy hanging onto

15:30.660 --> 15:34.289
those hammocky deposits of
gin sugars you call buttocks?"

15:34.414 --> 15:37.751
- What was that? What did you just write?
- Give me that.

15:37.835 --> 15:43.173
"Insecurity. Gender confusion. "
I'll give you something to write about.

15:43.257 --> 15:47.552
Look at me. I'm insane!
I'm Martin Lawrence on a bender.

15:52.850 --> 15:56.394
Mr and Mrs Griffin, does Stewart
have a history of aggression?

15:56.394 --> 15:59.941
No. Hitting Peter is the first
violent thing he's ever done.

15:59.941 --> 16:05.154
Technically, the first was that time bomb
I left ticking in your uterus before I came out.

16:05.279 --> 16:07.573
Happy 50th birthday, Lois.

16:07.656 --> 16:10.783
Your son is learning
misbehaviour from someone.

16:10.909 --> 16:14.455
I... I know who's responsible
for Stewie's behaviour,

16:14.538 --> 16:16.958
but if I told you,
Lois'd beat the crap out of me.

16:17.041 --> 16:21.212
Now, just a minute! The whole reason
I started fighting is because of you.

16:21.337 --> 16:26.133
I felt weak. You never listen to me.
You undermine me in front of the kids.

16:26.217 --> 16:29.553
And besides, you're not exactly
Father of the Year yourself.

16:29.679 --> 16:32.890
Well, there seems to be a lot
of anger in your household.

16:33.015 --> 16:36.352
You owe it to your son to learn
how to manage these feelings.

16:36.435 --> 16:37.603
Manage what?

16:39.272 --> 16:42.067
I know I went a little overboard
with my tae-jitsu,

16:42.192 --> 16:45.945
but from now on we're not gonna have
any more anger in this house, OK?

16:46.029 --> 16:49.073
Tell Chris to quit drawing
pictures of me with a pig's body.

16:49.156 --> 16:51.784
- Don't censure me!
- No more anger!

16:51.868 --> 16:58.333
OK. The psychologist wants us
to try an exercise called role reversal,

16:58.458 --> 17:02.211
where we pretend to be
the person who makes us angry.

17:02.295 --> 17:03.754
I'll go first.

17:03.880 --> 17:07.509
"Don't listen to your mother, kids.
She's worthless and dumb. "

17:07.634 --> 17:11.180
"Lgnore her and only listen to me - Peter. "

17:11.263 --> 17:16.059
"I'm Lois. I brake for yard sales,
but I don't let Peter buy anything he likes,

17:16.059 --> 17:20.021
like that Narragansett beer sign
where the hot chick has two mugs for jugs. "

17:20.146 --> 17:23.775
It was eight freakin' dollars,
and we have a dozen places to put it!

17:23.900 --> 17:25.027
Me next, me next!

17:25.152 --> 17:29.113
"I'm the dog. I'm well-read
and have a diverse stock portfolio,

17:29.196 --> 17:34.327
but I'm not above eating grass clippings and
regurgitating them on the rug by the door. "

17:34.411 --> 17:38.707
"I'm a pompous antichrist who will probably
drop my plans for world domination

17:38.791 --> 17:42.335
when I grow up and fall in love
with a rough trick named Jim. "

17:54.972 --> 17:56.433
Whoa, Peter, calm down.

17:56.516 --> 18:00.478
I'm sick of Lois's anger-management
techniques. They're not working.

18:00.604 --> 18:03.608
What about writing angry letters
and not sending them?

18:03.733 --> 18:07.360
- I wasn't supposed to send those?
- I got a letter from Dad.

18:07.485 --> 18:13.117
"Dear Meg. For the first four years of your
life, I thought you were a house cat. " Dad!

18:13.200 --> 18:15.912
"Dear Stewie. Get out. " That's nice.

18:15.912 --> 18:20.916
Mine just says "Dear Lois. " And after that
it looks like someone just spit on the paper.

18:20.916 --> 18:24.169
- You got somethin' to say to me?
- Yeah. PS:

18:27.714 --> 18:29.801
Hold on a sec.

18:30.426 --> 18:32.511
Hold on. Relax. Everybody, relax.

18:32.595 --> 18:34.888
I was hoping it wouldn't come to this,

18:34.888 --> 18:38.433
but we need to get our anger under control
before we kill each other.

18:38.433 --> 18:41.145
My psychiatrist gave me
these mood elevators.

18:41.145 --> 18:43.648
I think they could help even us out.

18:43.773 --> 18:46.775
